TieredVol-DRIVER — External References & Acknowledgments
=========================================================

TieredVol references and adapts techniques from the following open-source
projects and academic publications:

dm-stripe (Linux kernel)
  Weighted striping dispatch — boundary-array based disk selection.
  drivers/md/dm-stripe.c

dm-switch (Linux kernel)
  Region-based bio dispatch with random fallback for degraded/stale disks.
  drivers/md/dm-switch.c

dm-crypt (Linux kernel)
  Bio clone + sector remapping + custom end_io completion handler.
  drivers/md/dm-crypt.c

dm-linear (Linux kernel)
  Two-line bio remapping pattern: bio_set_dev() + bi_sector rewrite.
  drivers/md/dm-linear.c

dm-raid1 (Linux kernel)
  Mirror write via bio_alloc_clone, per-CPU pending tracking, read retry.
  drivers/md/dm-raid1.c

dm-dust (Linux kernel)
  Time-based stale disk detection and automatic skip during dispatch.
  drivers/md/dm-dust.c

dm-log-writes (Linux kernel)
  Structured I/O event logging via kfifo ring buffer with typed entries.
  drivers/md/dm-log-writes.c

blk-mq (Linux kernel)
  Per-disk I/O statistics: inflight bytes, read/write ops/bytes, latency.
  block/blk-mq.c

emlog by nicupavel
  Fixed-size kernel ring buffer for structured event logging (design concept).
  https://github.com/nicupavel/emlog

Jiao & Kim, "Asymmetric RAID: Rethinking RAID for SSD Heterogeneity"
  HotStorage'24 — multi-factor adaptive dispatch (load, latency, wear).
  https://doi.org/10.1145/3655038.3665947
